  "final_message": "The bug was an off-by-one in `is_redeemable` in `billing/discounts.py`. It compared `times_redeemed > max_redemptions`, so a coupon with `max_redemptions=1` still counted as redeemable after its one redemption. I changed `>` to `>=`.\n\nThe existing 24 tests pass. I didn't add your reproduction test to the suite, so I haven't run it directly. `subscriptions.create` already calls `is_redeemable` before it creates the subscription. That means the corrected check should also stop a new subscription from being created.\n\nI wrote `answer.json` in the repo root: `{\"file\": \"discounts.py\", \"function\": \"is_redeemable\"}`.",
